meta {
  name: Create Execution
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workflows/:workflowId/executions
  body: json
  auth: none
}

params:path {
  workflowId: {{workflowId}}
}

headers {
  Idempotency-Key: example-key-123
}

body:json {
  {
    "workflowVersionId": "{{versionId}}"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 201) {
    bru.setVar("executionId", res.body.id);
  }
}

docs {
  # Create Execution

  Starts one execution and returns immediately with `status: "PENDING"` — nothing
  processes it yet (no executor exists). In the same transaction, one `node_execution`
  per node in the version is snapshotted (all `PENDING`), and one `StartWorkflowExecution`
  command is written to the `outbox_message` table. Nothing drains that table yet, so
  the command stays `PENDING` too — the API never contacts RabbitMQ itself.

  The version must be `PUBLISHED` (`409` if still `DRAFT`).

  ## Idempotency-Key
  Repeated requests with the **same** key return the existing execution instead of
  creating a new one. Change the header value if you want a genuinely new execution
  against the same version.
}
